[
  {
    "sha": "b0e121cefc262a5c641aa06e0677334515a73a9a",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGIwZTEyMWNlZmMyNjJhNWM2NDFhYTA2ZTA2NzczMzQ1MTVhNzNhOWE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T09:40:59Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T09:40:59Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(edm): sinker electrode wear compensation in Z\n\nA stated axial wear rate - a condition's `wear` in the .mch edm\ncondition table, or a wear measured on the op between burns (length\nlost over depth burned, which wins) - deepens each burn layer by the\nrate times the depth burned by then. With neither stated the burn is\nnot compensated and its path and page say so. A rate that is not a\nfinite ratio in [0, 1) is refused by name at the machine file and at\nCreateOperation / EditOperationParams; every layer move is bounded by\nthe stated floor plus the compensation and an over-deep move refuses\nby name. The stock sim judges the worn electrode's burn. Additive DTO\nkeys: older files load unchanged. Golden sinker_wear_layers.cl.\n\nFixes #546\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "981db1f9ca19ffecf15341f9dba86189fe33b5a9",
