  {
    "sha": "9f0c42f85ad2dbd08bda36ed98bc82b9255aec05",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDlmMGM0MmY4NWFkMmRiZDA4YmRhMzZlZDk4YmM4MmI5MjU1YWVjMDU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T19:34:49Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T19:34:49Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): refuse a sinker wear rate on a wire EDM machine by name\n\n`wear` (#546) is a sinker-only condition field. A wire machine stating\nit was read and ignored; it is now refused by condition id and key,\nthe same as `undersize`, and `Edm::fits` counts a stated wear as a\nsinker key so a hand-edited parsed machine is not sane either. Pinned\nby a_wear_rate_is_a_sinker_field (post) and\na_wire_machine_stating_wear_is_refused_by_name (app). The decision\nfile notes that a misstated rate is not caught by the sim.\n\nRefs #546\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
