        "date": "2026-11-13T01:07:26Z"
      },
      "message": "Merge upstream/main into issue/546-sinker-wear-comp (orbit #544, side burn #545)\n\nHand resolution, author's decision (docs/decisions/546-sinker-wear-comp.md,\n\"merge with orbit and side burn\"):\n- SinkerBurnOp keeps main's orbit and this PR's layer/wear fields; is_sane\n  checks both; constructors, DTO and fixtures carry both.\n- The orbit runs at each layer's wear-compensated tip in\n  sinker_wear::burn_compensated, judged against the deepest compensated\n  tip and the worn-tip electrode-length law; with no rate the moves are\n  main's burn_to_depth.\n- A Sinker Side Burn stating a wear rate or layer step is refused by name\n  (SinkerSideBurnOp::refusal: create, edit, paste, change-kind, reader,\n  generator). Follow-up #1340.\n- The stock sim maps both ends of a move to the worn electrode, so a worn\n  orbit's level moves are judged at the burned floor.\n- The params digest writes orbit, then tagged wear, then side bytes; the\n  sinker-wear stamp term stays beside the other sinker digests.\n\nRefs #546\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
